  <name>kmd</name>
  <summary>Beautiful Markdown previews in the terminal</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      kmd renders Markdown documents as rich, colorful previews directly in
      your terminal. It is a single small binary without dependencies that
      starts in a few milliseconds.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Full CommonMark 0.31.2 and GitHub Flavored Markdown support</li>
      <li>Emoji shortcodes and wiki links between documents</li>
      <li>Syntax highlighting for more than 20 languages</li>
      <li>Clickable hyperlinks and inline images</li>
      <li>Mermaid (flowchart, state, sequence, class, ER, Gantt, pie) and Graphviz diagrams drawn with Unicode box characters</li>
      <li>LaTeX math formulas rendered with Unicode</li>
      <li>Thirteen bundled color themes and fully customizable themes</li>
      <li>A viewer that follows links between documents and folders, with a table of contents and search</li>
      <li>Live preview, presentation mode, single-section output and HTML export</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
